    = 1.000846453470\n    p 95% CI     = [1.000664436785, 1.001014712471]\n    contains 1   = False\n\nProfile theta_c:\n    best = -29.316126653307 deg\n    95% CI = [-29.316126653307,\n              -29.316126653307] deg\n\nExact dynamical identity:\n    C_tau = 6.935100477359e-15\n    relative std = 2.684917585972e-16\n\nTau reconstruction:\n    RMSE_log = 5.534813274224e-05\n\nIMPORTANT:\n    tau and xi0 are not treated as independent datasets.\n    The tau reconstruction follows algebraically from the\n    exact identity and is therefore an internal consistency\n    test, not an independent likelihood contribution.\n\n================================================================================\nFILES SAVED\n================================================================================\n/kaggle/working/krasilnikov_critical_audit_v3/bootstrap_p_distribution.png\n/kaggle/working/krasilnikov_critical_audit_v3/bootstrap_theta_c_vs_p.png\n/kaggle/working/krasilnikov_critical_audit_v3/critical_audit_consistency.csv\n/kaggle/working/krasilnikov_critical_audit_v3/critical_bootstrap_parameters.csv\n/kaggle/working/krasilnikov_critical_audit_v3/critical_bootstrap_summary.csv\n/kaggle/working/krasilnikov_critical_audit_v3/critical_fit_comparison.csv\n/kaggle/working/krasilnikov_critical_audit_v3/critical_pointwise_diagnostics.csv\n/kaggle/working/krasilnikov_critical_audit_v3/critical_residuals.png\n/kaggle/working/krasilnikov_critical_audit_v3/critical_scaling_fit.png\n/kaggle/working/krasilnikov_critical_audit_v3/theta_c_profile.csv\n/kaggle/working/krasilnikov_critical_audit_v3/theta_c_profile_likelihood.png\n\nDONE.\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":15},{"cell_type":"code","source":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\n\n\"\"\"\nKRASILNIKOV EQ. (8)\nADAPTIVE PROFILE-LIKELIHOOD AUDIT\n=================================\n\nObiettivi\n---------\n\n1. Fit terminale:\n       xi0(theta) = A * (theta_c-theta)^(-p) + B\n\n2. Fit ristretto:\n       p = 1\n\n3. Profilo adattivo di theta_c:\n       profile_RSS(theta_c)\n   ottimizzando A, p, B.\n\n4. Profilo adattivo di p:\n       profile_RSS(p)\n   ottimizzando A, theta_c, B.\n\n5. Determinazione numerica dei limiti CI tramite:\n       LR(parameter) = N log(RSS_profile / RSS_min)\n\n   e soglia:\n       chi2_1(0.95) = 3.841459\n\n6. Likelihood-ratio test p=1.\n\n7. Parametric Monte Carlo del test p=1:\n   genera dati dal modello libero e misura la distribuzione\n   empirica della statistica LR.\n\n8. Bootstrap residuo a disegno theta fisso.\n\n9. Verifica dell'identità dinamica:\n       tau_p * xi0 * exp(-E) = C_tau\n\n10. Ricostruzione dinamica:\n       tau_pred = C_tau exp(E) / xi_fit\n\nIMPORTANTE\n----------\n\n- theta e' mantenuto fisso nel bootstrap.\n- xi0 e tau_p NON sono trattati come due dataset indipendenti.\n- Il tau viene usato solo come verifica deterministica.\n- Non vengono utilizzate spline.\n- Nessuna interpolazione attraversa il gap theta=-29.32 -> -21.18.\n- theta_c e' esterno al supporto direttamente osservato.\n- Le CI profile sono ottenute tramite root-finding adattivo,\n  non da una griglia uniforme.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport os\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n\nfrom scipy.optimize import least_squares, brentq\nfrom scipy.stats import chi2\n\n# ============================================================\n# CONFIG\n# ============================================================\n\nTHETA_MIN = -29.60\nTHETA_MAX = -29.32\n\nRANDOM_SEED = 20260914\n\nN_BOOT = 5000\nN_MC_LR = 3000\n\nOUTPUT_DIR = \"/kaggle/working/krasilnikov_critical_audit_v4\"\nos.makedirs(OUTPUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\nrng = np.random.default_rng(RANDOM_SEED)\n\nCHI2_95 = chi2.ppf(0.95, 1)\n\n\n# ============================================================\n# 1. FIND INPUT CSV\n# ============================================================\n\nTARGET = \"krasilnikov_eq8_theta_scan_physical.csv\"\n\nmatches = []\n\nfor root, dirs, files in os.walk(\"/kaggle/input\"):\n    for f in files:\n        if f == TARGET:\n            matches.append(os.path.join(root, f))\n\nif not matches:\n\n    for root, dirs, files in os.walk(\"/kaggle/input\"):\n\n        for f in files:\n\n            if not f.lower().endswith(\".csv\"):\n                continue\n\n            path = os.path.join(root, f)\n\n            try:\n                cols = pd.read_csv(\n                    path,\n                    nrows=2\n                ).columns\n\n                required = {\n                    \"theta_deg\",\n                    \"xi0\",\n                    \"tau_p_s\",\n                    \"exponent\"\n                }\n\n                if required.issubset(set(cols)):\n                    matches.append(path)\n\n            except Exception:\n                pass\n\n\nif not matches:\n    raise FileNotFoundError(\n        \"No compatible Krasilnikov CSV found.\"\n    )\n\nDATA_PATH = matches[0]\n\nprint(\"=\" * 80)\nprint(\"INPUT\")\nprint(\"=\" * 80)\nprint(DATA_PATH)\n\n\n# ============================================================\n# 2. LOAD DATA\n# ============================================================\n\ndf = pd.read_csv(DATA_PATH)\n\nrequired = [\n    \"theta_deg\",\n    \"xi0\",\n    \"tau_p_s\",\n    \"exponent\"\n]\n\nmissing = [\n    c for c in required\n    if c not in df.columns\n]\n\nif missing:\n    raise ValueError(\n        f\"Missing columns: {missing}\"\n    )\n\ndf = df.copy()\n\ndf = df[\n    np.isfinite(df[\"theta_deg\"]) &\n    np.isfinite(df[\"xi0\"]) &\n    np.isfinite(df[\"tau_p_s\"]) &\n    np.isfinite(df[\"exponent\"])\n]\n\ndf = df[\n    (df[\"xi0\"] > 0) &\n    (df[\"tau_p_s\"] > 0)\n]\n\ndf = df.sort_values(\n    \"theta_deg\"\n).reset_index(drop=True)\n\n\n# ============================================================\n# 3. TERMINAL BRANCH\n# ============================================================\n\nbranch = df[\n    (df[\"theta_deg\"] >= THETA_MIN) &\n    (df[\"theta_deg\"] <= THETA_MAX)\n].copy()\n\nbranch = branch.sort_values(\n    \"theta_deg\"\n).reset_index(drop=True)\n\ntheta = branch[\"theta_deg\"].to_numpy(float)\nxi = branch[\"xi0\"].to_numpy(float)\ntau = branch[\"tau_p_s\"].to_numpy(float)\nE = branch[\"exponent\"].to_numpy(float)\n\ny = np.log(xi)\n\nN = len(theta)\n\ntheta_last = np.max(theta)\n\nprint(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 80)\nprint(\"TERMINAL BRANCH\")\nprint(\"=\" * 80)\n\nprint(f\"N             = {N}\")\nprint(f\"theta_min     = {theta.min():.12f}\")\nprint(f\"theta_max     = {theta.max():.12f}\")\n\n\n# ============================================================\n# 4. MODELS\n# ============================================================\n\ndef xi_model(theta, A, theta_c, p, B):\n\n    delta = theta_c - theta\n\n    if np.any(delta <= 0):\n        return np.full_like(\n            theta,\n            np.nan,\n            dtype=float\n        )\n\n    value = (\n        A * delta ** (-p)\n        + B\n    )\n\n    if np.any(value <= 0):\n        return np.full_like(\n            theta,\n            np.nan,\n            dtype=float\n        )\n\n    return value\n\n\n# ============================================================\n# 5. FREE FIT\n# ============================================================\n\ndef residual_free(\n    pars,\n    theta_data,\n    y_data\n):\n\n    A, theta_c, p, B = pars\n\n    pred = xi_model(\n        theta_data,\n        A,\n        theta_c,\n        p,\n        B\n    )\n\n    if np.any(~np.isfinite(pred)):\n        return np.full_like(\n            y_data,\n            1e6\n        )\n\n    return np.log(pred) - y_data\n\n\nx0 = np.array([\n    19.83,\n    -29.31614,\n    1.0008,\n    5.53\n])\n\nlower = np.array([\n    1e-10,\n    theta_last + 1e-10,\n    0.05,\n    -100.0\n])\n\nupper = np.array([\n    1e6,\n    theta_last + 1.0,\n    5.0,\n    1e4\n])\n\nfit = least_squares(\n    residual_free,\n    x0,\n    args=(theta, y),\n    bounds=(lower, upper),\n    max_nfev=100000,\n    xtol=1e-14,\n    ftol=1e-14,\n    gtol=1e-14\n)\n\nA_hat, theta_c_hat, p_hat, B_hat = fit.x\n\nxi_hat = xi_model(\n    theta,\n    A_hat,\n    theta_c_hat,\n    p_hat,\n    B_hat\n)\n\nr_hat = np.log(xi_hat) - y\n\nRSS_hat = np.sum(r_hat**2)\n\nRMSE_hat = np.sqrt(\n    RSS_hat / N\n)\n\n\n# ============================================================\n# 6. p=1 FIT\n# ============================================================\n\ndef residual_p1(\n    pars,\n    theta_data,\n    y_data\n):\n\n    A, theta_c, B = pars\n\n    pred = xi_model(\n        theta_data,\n        A,\n        theta_c,\n        1.0,\n        B\n    )\n\n    if np.any(~np.isfinite(pred)):\n        return np.full_like(\n            y_data,\n            1e6\n        )\n\n    return np.log(pred) - y_data\n\n\nfit_p1 = least_squares(\n    residual_p1,\n    [\n        A_hat,\n        theta_c_hat,\n        B_hat\n    ],\n    args=(theta, y),\n    bounds=(\n        [\n            1e-10,\n            theta_last + 1e-10,\n            -100\n        ],\n        [\n            1e6,\n            theta_last + 1.0,\n            1e4\n        ]\n    ),\n    max_nfev=100000,\n    xtol=1e-14,\n    ftol=1e-14,\n    gtol=1e-14\n)\n\nA1, theta_c_1, B1 = fit_p1.x\n\nxi_1 = xi_model(\n    theta,\n    A1,\n    theta_c_1,\n    1.0,\n    B1\n)\n\nr1 = np.log(xi_1) - y\n\nRSS_1 = np.sum(r1**2)\n\nRMSE_1 = np.sqrt(\n    RSS_1 / N\n)\n\n\n# ============================================================\n# 7. AIC/BIC/LR\n# ============================================================\n\nk_free = 4\nk_p1 = 3\n\nAIC_free = (\n    N * np.log(RSS_hat / N)\n    + 2 * k_free\n)\n\nAIC_p1 = (\n    N * np.log(RSS_1 / N)\n    + 2 * k_p1\n)\n\nBIC_free = (\n    N * np.log(RSS_hat / N)\n    + k_free * np.log(N)\n)\n\nBIC_p1 = (\n    N * np.log(RSS_1 / N)\n    + k_p1 * np.log(N)\n)\n\nLR_observed = (\n    N * np.log(\n        RSS_1 / RSS_hat\n    )\n)\n\nLR_asymptotic_pvalue = chi2.sf(\n    LR_observed,\n    1\n)\n\n\n# ============================================================\n# 8. PROFILE: FIX theta_c\n# ============================================================\n\ndef fit_given_theta_c(\n    theta_c_fixed\n):\n\n    def residual(pars):\n\n        A, p, B = pars\n\n        pred = xi_model(\n            theta,\n            A,\n            theta_c_fixed,\n            p,\n            B\n        )\n\n        if np.any(~np.isfinite(pred)):\n            return np.full(\n                N,\n                1e6\n            )\n\n        return np.log(pred) - y\n\n    result = least_squares(\n        residual,\n        [\n            A_hat,\n            p_hat,\n            B_hat\n        ],\n        bounds=(\n            [\n                1e-10,\n                0.05,\n                -100\n            ],\n            [\n                1e6,\n                5.0,\n                1e4\n            ]\n        ),\n        max_nfev=50000,\n        xtol=1e-12,\n        ftol=1e-12,\n        gtol=1e-12\n    )\n\n    rss = np.sum(\n        result.fun**2\n    )\n\n    return rss, result.x\n\n\ndef theta_c_profile_LR(\n    tc\n):\n\n    rss, _ = fit_given_theta_c(tc)\n\n    return N * np.log(\n        rss / RSS_hat\n    )\n\n\n# ============================================================\n# 9. ADAPTIVE THETA_c PROFILE\n# ============================================================\n\nprint(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 80)\nprint(\"ADAPTIVE PROFILE theta_c\")\nprint(\"=\" * 80)\n\n# Dense exploratory grid ONLY to locate crossings.\n# Root finding is then performed continuously.\n\ntc_grid_left = np.linspace(\n    theta_last + 1e-7,\n    theta_c_hat - 1e-8,\n    120\n)\n\ntc_grid_right = np.linspace(\n    theta_c_hat + 1e-8,\n    theta_c_hat + 0.05,\n    160\n)\n\ntc_grid = np.unique(\n    np.concatenate([\n        tc_grid_left,\n        tc_grid_right\n    ])\n)\n\ntc_grid.sort()\n\ntc_LR = np.array([\n    theta_c_profile_LR(tc)\n    for tc in tc_grid\n])\n\n# left crossing\nleft_mask = tc_grid < theta_c_hat\n\nleft_grid = tc_grid[left_mask]\nleft_lr = tc_LR[left_mask]\n\nleft_cross = None\n\nfor i in range(len(left_grid) - 1):\n\n    if (\n        left_lr[i] - CHI2_95\n    ) * (\n        left_lr[i + 1] - CHI2_95\n    ) <= 0:\n\n        left_cross = brentq(\n            lambda tc:\n                theta_c_profile_LR(tc)\n                - CHI2_95,\n            left_grid[i],\n            left_grid[i + 1],\n            xtol=1e-12,\n            rtol=1e-12\n        )\n\n        break\n\n\n# right crossing\nright_mask = tc_grid > theta_c_hat\n\nright_grid = tc_grid[right_mask]\nright_lr = tc_LR[right_mask]\n\nright_cross = None\n\nfor i in range(len(right_grid) - 1):\n\n    if (\n        right_lr[i] - CHI2_95\n    ) * (\n        right_lr[i + 1] - CHI2_95\n    ) <= 0:\n\n        right_cross = brentq(\n            lambda tc:\n                theta_c_profile_LR(tc)\n                - CHI2_95,\n            right_grid[i],\n            right_grid[i + 1],\n            xtol=1e-12,\n            rtol=1e-12\n        )\n\n        break\n\n\n# ============================================================\n# 10. PROFILE: FIX p\n# ============================================================\n\ndef fit_given_p(\n    p_fixed\n):\n\n    def residual(pars):\n\n        A, theta_c, B = pars\n\n        pred = xi_model(\n            theta,\n            A,\n            theta_c,\n            p_fixed,\n            B\n        )\n\n        if np.any(~np.isfinite(pred)):\n            return np.full(\n                N,\n                1e6\n            )\n\n        return np.log(pred) - y\n\n    result = least_squares(\n        residual,\n        [\n            A_hat,\n            theta_c_hat,\n            B_hat\n        ],\n        bounds=(\n            [\n                1e-10,\n                theta_last + 1e-10,\n                -100\n            ],\n            [\n                1e6,\n                theta_last + 1.0,\n                1e4\n            ]\n        ),\n        max_nfev=50000,\n        xtol=1e-12,\n        ftol=1e-12,\n        gtol=1e-12\n    )\n\n    rss = np.sum(\n        result.fun**2\n    )\n\n    return rss, result.x\n\n\ndef p_profile_LR(p_fixed):\n\n    rss, _ = fit_given_p(\n        p_fixed\n    )\n\n    return N * np.log(\n        rss / RSS_hat\n    )\n\n\n# ============================================================\n# 11. ADAPTIVE p PROFILE\n# ============================================================\n\nprint(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 80)\nprint(\"ADAPTIVE PROFILE p\")\nprint(\"=\" * 80)\n\np_grid = np.linspace(\n    0.90,\n    1.10,\n    161\n)\n\np_LR = np.array([\n    p_profile_LR(pv)\n    for pv in p_grid\n])\n\n\n# Find crossings on left and right\n\np_left = p_grid[\n    p_grid < p_hat\n]\n\nlr_left = p_LR[\n    p_grid < p_hat\n]\n\np_right = p_grid[\n    p_grid > p_hat\n]\n\nlr_right = p_LR[\n    p_grid > p_hat\n]\n\np_left_cross = None\np_right_cross = None\n\n\nfor i in range(len(p_left) - 1):\n\n    if (\n        lr_left[i] - CHI2_95\n    ) * (\n        lr_left[i + 1] - CHI2_95\n    ) <= 0:\n\n        p_left_cross = brentq(\n            lambda pv:\n                p_profile_LR(pv)\n                - CHI2_95,\n            p_left[i],\n            p_left[i + 1],\n            xtol=1e-11,\n            rtol=1e-11\n        )\n\n        break\n\n\nfor i in range(len(p_right) - 1):\n\n    if (\n        lr_right[i] - CHI2_95\n    ) * (\n        lr_right[i + 1] - CHI2_95\n    ) <= 0:\n\n        p_right_cross = brentq(\n            lambda pv:\n                p_profile_LR(pv)\n                - CHI2_95,\n            p_right[i],\n            p_right[i + 1],\n            xtol=1e-11,\n            rtol=1e-11\n        )\n\n        break\n\n\n# ============================================================\n# 12. EXACT DYNAMIC IDENTITY\n# ============================================================\n\nC_tau_values = (\n    tau * xi * np.exp(-E)\n)\n\nC_tau = np.mean(\n    C_tau_values\n)\n\nC_tau_rel_std = (\n    np.std(\n        C_tau_values,\n        ddof=1\n    ) / abs(C_tau)\n)\n\ntau_pred = (\n    C_tau\n    * np.exp(E)\n    / xi_hat\n)\n\ntau_log_residual = (\n    np.log(tau_pred)\n    - np.log(tau)\n)\n\ntau_RMSE = np.sqrt(\n    np.mean(\n        tau_log_residual**2\n    )\n)\n\n\n# ============================================================\n# 13. RESIDUAL BOOTSTRAP\n# ============================================================\n\nprint(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 80)\nprint(\"RESIDUAL BOOTSTRAP\")\nprint(\"=\" * 80)\n\nr_centered = (\n    r_hat - np.mean(r_hat)\n)\n\nboot_rows = []\n\nfor b in range(N_BOOT):\n\n    eps = rng.choice(\n        r_centered,\n        size=N,\n        replace=True\n    )\n\n    y_b = (\n        np.log(xi_hat)\n        + eps\n    )\n\n    try:\n\n        fit_b = least_squares(\n            residual_free,\n            [\n                A_hat,\n                theta_c_hat,\n                p_hat,\n                B_hat\n            ],\n            args=(theta, y_b),\n            bounds=(\n                lower,\n                upper\n            ),\n            max_nfev=30000,\n            xtol=1e-11,\n            ftol=1e-11,\n            gtol=1e-11\n        )\n\n        if not fit_b.success:\n            continue\n\n        A_b, tc_b, p_b, B_b = fit_b.x\n\n        if (\n            np.isfinite(A_b)\n            and np.isfinite(tc_b)\n            and np.isfinite(p_b)\n            and np.isfinite(B_b)\n        ):\n\n            boot_rows.append({\n                \"bootstrap\": b,\n                \"A\": A_b,\n                \"theta_c\": tc_b,\n                \"p\": p_b,\n                \"B\": B_b\n            })\n\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n\n\nboot = pd.DataFrame(\n    boot_rows\n)\n\n\n# ============================================================\n# 14. PARAMETRIC MONTE CARLO LR TEST\n# ============================================================\n\n\"\"\"\nNull hypothesis:\n\n    H0: p = 1\n\nWe simulate data from the fitted p=1 model with the same theta\ndesign and Gaussian log residual variance estimated from the\nrestricted model.\n\nFor every synthetic dataset:\n\n    LR_MC =\n        N log(RSS_p1 / RSS_free)\n\nThe empirical p-value is the fraction of LR_MC >= observed LR.\n\"\"\"\n\nprint(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 80)\nprint(\"PARAMETRIC MONTE CARLO LR TEST\")\nprint(\"=\" * 80)\n\nsigma0 = np.sqrt(\n    RSS_1 / N\n)\n\nxi_null = xi_1.copy()\n\nLR_mc = []\n\nfor m in range(N_MC_LR):\n\n    noise = rng.normal(\n        0.0,\n        sigma0,\n        size=N\n    )\n\n    y_mc = (\n        np.log(xi_null)\n        + noise\n    )\n\n    # Free model\n    try:\n\n        fm = least_squares(\n            residual_free,\n            [\n                A1,\n                theta_c_1,\n                1.0,\n                B1\n            ],\n            args=(theta, y_mc),\n            bounds=(\n                lower,\n                upper\n            ),\n            max_nfev=20000,\n            xtol=1e-10,\n            ftol=1e-10,\n            gtol=1e-10\n        )\n\n        if not fm.success:\n            continue\n\n        pars_free_mc = fm.x\n\n        pred_free_mc = xi_model(\n            theta,\n            *pars_free_mc\n        )\n\n        if np.any(\n            ~np.isfinite(pred_free_mc)\n        ):\n            continue\n\n        rss_free_mc = np.sum(\n            (\n                np.log(pred_free_mc)\n                - y_mc\n            )**2\n        )\n\n        # Restricted model\n        def res_mc_p1(pars):\n\n            pred = xi_model(\n                theta,\n                pars[0],\n                pars[1],\n                1.0,\n                pars[2]\n            )\n\n            if np.any(\n                ~np.isfinite(pred)\n            ):\n                return np.full(\n                    N,\n                    1e6\n                )\n\n            return (\n                np.log(pred)\n                - y_mc\n            )\n\n        rm = least_squares(\n            res_mc_p1,\n            [\n                A1,\n                theta_c_1,\n                B1\n            ],\n            bounds=(\n                [\n                    1e-10,\n                    theta_last + 1e-10,\n                    -100\n                ],\n                [\n                    1e6,\n                    theta_last + 1.0,\n                    1e4\n                ]\n            ),\n            max_nfev=20000,\n            xtol=1e-10,\n            ftol=1e-10,\n            gtol=1e-10\n        )\n\n        if not rm.success:\n            continue\n\n        rss_p1_mc = np.sum(\n            rm.fun**2\n        )\n\n        lr_mc = (\n            N\n            * np.log(\n                rss_p1_mc\n                / rss_free_mc\n            )\n        )\n\n        if np.isfinite(lr_mc):\n            LR_mc.append(lr_mc)\n\n    except Exception:\n        continue\n\n\nLR_mc = np.asarray(LR_mc)\n\nmc_pvalue = np.mean(\n    LR_mc >= LR_observed\n)\n\n\n# ============================================================\n# 15. SAVE PROFILE theta_c\n# ============================================================\n\ntheta_profile_rows = []\n\nfor tc, lr in zip(\n    tc_grid,\n    tc_LR\n):\n\n    rss, pars = fit_given_theta_c(\n        tc\n    )\n\n    theta_profile_rows.append({\n        \"theta_c\": tc,\n        \"RSS\": rss,\n        \"LR\": lr,\n        \"A\": pars[0],\n        \"p\": pars[1],\n        \"B\": pars[2]\n    })\n\ntheta_profile_df = pd.DataFrame(\n    theta_profile_rows\n)\n\ntheta_profile_df.to_csv(\n    os.path.join(\n        OUTPUT_DIR,\n        \"adaptive_theta_c_profile.csv\"\n    ),\n    index=False\n)\n\n\n# ============================================================\n# 16. SAVE PROFILE p\n# ============================================================\n\np_profile_rows = []\n\nfor pv, lr in zip(\n    p_grid,\n    p_LR\n):\n\n    rss, pars = fit_given_p(\n        pv\n    )\n\n    p_profile_rows.append({\n        \"p\": pv,\n        \"RSS\": rss,\n        \"LR\": lr,\n        \"A\": pars[0],\n        \"theta_c\": pars[1],\n        \"B\": pars[2]\n    })\n\np_profile_df = pd.DataFrame(\n    p_profile_rows\n)\n\np_profile_df.to_csv(\n    os.path.join(\n        OUTPUT_DIR,\n        \"adaptive_p_profile.csv\"\n    ),\n    index=False\n)\n\n\n# ============================================================\n# 17. SAVE BOOTSTRAP\n# ============================================================\n\nboot.to_csv(\n    os.path.join(\n        OUTPUT_DIR,\n        \"bootstrap_parameters.csv\"\n    ),\n    index=False\n)\n\n\n# ============================================================\n# 18. SAVE MC LR\n# ============================================================\n\npd.DataFrame({\n    \"LR_MC\": LR_mc\n}).to_csv(\n    os.path.join(\n        OUTPUT_DIR,\n        \"monte_carlo_LR.csv\"\n    ),\n    index=False\n)\n\n\n# ============================================================\n# 19. BOOTSTRAP SUMMARY\n# ============================================================\n\ndef q025(series):\n    return np.quantile(\n        series,\n        0.025\n    )\n\n\ndef q975(series):\n    return np.quantile(\n        series,\n        0.975\n    )\n\n\nboot_summary = pd.DataFrame([\n    {\n        \"parameter\": c,\n        \"mean\": boot[c].mean(),\n        \"median\": boot[c].median(),\n        \"std\": boot[c].std(ddof=1),\n        \"q025\": q025(boot[c]),\n        \"q975\": q975(boot[c])\n    }\n    for c in [\n        \"A\",\n        \"theta_c\",\n        \"p\",\n        \"B\"\n    ]\n])\n\nboot_summary.to_csv(\n    os.path.join(\n        OUTPUT_DIR,\n        \"bootstrap_summary.csv\"\n    ),\n    index=False\n)\n\n\n# ============================================================\n# 20. CONSISTENCY TABLE\n# ============================================================\n\nconsistency = pd.DataFrame([{\n\n    \"N\": N,\n\n    \"theta_last\":\n        theta_last,\n\n    \"A_hat\":\n        A_hat,\n\n    \"theta_c_hat\":\n        theta_c_hat,\n\n    \"p_hat\":\n        p_hat,\n\n    \"B_hat\":\n        B_hat,\n\n    \"theta_c_offset\":\n        theta_c_hat - theta_last,\n\n    \"A_p1\":\n        A1,\n\n    \"theta_c_p1\":\n        theta_c_1,\n\n    \"B_p1\":\n        B1,\n\n    \"RSS_free\":\n        RSS_hat,\n\n    \"RSS_p1\":\n        RSS_1,\n\n    \"RMSE_free\":\n        RMSE_hat,\n\n    \"RMSE_p1\":\n        RMSE_1,\n\n    \"AIC_free\":\n        AIC_free,\n\n    \"AIC_p1\":\n        AIC_p1,\n\n    \"BIC_free\":\n        BIC_free,\n\n    \"BIC_p1\":\n        BIC_p1,\n\n    \"LR_observed\":\n        LR_observed,\n\n    \"LR_asymptotic_pvalue\":\n        LR_asymptotic_pvalue,\n\n    \"LR_MC_pvalue\":\n        mc_pvalue,\n\n    \"N_MC\":\n        len(LR_mc),\n\n    \"theta_c_profile_low\":\n        left_cross\n        if left_cross is not None\n        else np.nan,\n\n    \"theta_c_profile_high\":\n        right_cross\n        if right_cross is not None\n        else np.nan,\n\n    \"p_profile_low\":\n        p_left_cross\n        if p_left_cross is not None\n        else np.nan,\n\n    \"p_profile_high\":\n        p_right_cross\n        if p_right_cross is not None\n        else np.nan,\n\n    \"profile_p_contains_1\":\n        (\n            p_left_cross is not None\n            and p_right_cross is not None\n            and p_left_cross <= 1.0 <= p_right_cross\n        ),\n\n    \"C_tau\":\n        C_tau,\n\n    \"C_tau_relative_std\":\n        C_tau_rel_std,\n\n    \"tau_reconstruction_RMSE_log\":\n        tau_RMSE,\n\n    \"bootstrap_success\":\n        len(boot) / N_BOOT,\n\n    \"bootstrap_p_q025\":\n        q025(boot[\"p\"]),\n\n    \"bootstrap_p_q975\":\n        q975(boot[\"p\"]),\n\n    \"bootstrap_theta_c_q025\":\n        q025(boot[\"theta_c\"]),\n\n    \"bootstrap_theta_c_q975\":\n        q975(boot[\"theta_c\"]),\n\n    \"bootstrap_corr_theta_c_p\":\n        np.corrcoef(\n            boot[\"theta_c\"],\n            boot[\"p\"]\n        )[0, 1]\n\n}])\n\nconsistency.to_csv(\n    os.path.join(\n        OUTPUT_DIR,\n        \"adaptive_audit_consistency.csv\"\n    ),\n    index=False\n)\n\n\n# ============================================================\n# 21. POINTWISE DIAGNOSTICS\n# ============================================================\n\ndiagnostics = branch.copy()\n\ndiagnostics[\"xi_fit\"] = xi_hat\ndiagnostics[\"xi_fit_p1\"] = xi_1\n\ndiagnostics[\"log_residual\"] = r_hat\ndiagnostics[\"log_residual_p1\"] = r1\n\ndiagnostics[\"tau_reconstructed\"] = tau_pred\n\ndiagnostics[\"tau_log_residual\"] = (\n    tau_log_residual\n)\n\ndiagnostics[\"C_tau_pointwise\"] = (\n    C_tau_values\n)\n\ndiagnostics.to_csv(\n    os.path.join(\n        OUTPUT_DIR,\n        \"pointwise_diagnostics.csv\"\n    ),\n    index=False\n)\n\n\n# ============================================================\n# 22. PLOT theta_c PROFILE\n# ============================================================\n\nplt.figure(\n    figsize=(9, 6)\n)\n\nplt.plot(\n    theta_profile_df[\"theta_c\"],\n    theta_profile_df[\"LR\"],\n    linewidth=2\n)\n\nplt.axhline(\n    CHI2_95,\n    linestyle=\"--\",\n    label=r\"$\\chi^2_1(0.95)$\"\n)\n\nplt.axvline(\n    theta_c_hat,\n    linestyle=\":\",\n    label=\"best fit\"\n)\n\nif left_cross is not None:\n    plt.axvline(\n        left_cross,\n        linestyle=\"--\"\n    )\n\nif right_cross is not None:\n    plt.axvline(\n        right_cross,\n        linestyle=\"--\"\n    )\n\nplt.xlabel(r\"$\\theta_c$ [deg]\")\nplt.ylabel(r\"$\\Lambda(\\theta_c)$\")\n\nplt.title(\n    r\"Adaptive profile likelihood: $\\theta_c$\"\n)\n\nplt.legend()\nplt.grid(\n    True,\n    alpha=0.3\n)\n\nplt.tight_layout()\n\nplt.savefig(\n    os.path.join(\n        OUTPUT_DIR,\n        \"adaptive_theta_c_profile.png\"\n    ),\n    dpi=220\n)\n\nplt.close()\n\n\n# ============================================================\n# 23. PLOT p PROFILE\n# ============================================================\n\nplt.figure(\n    figsize=(9, 6)\n)\n\nplt.plot(\n    p_profile_df[\"p\"],\n    p_profile_df[\"LR\"],\n    linewidth=2\n)\n\nplt.axhline(\n    CHI2_95,\n    linestyle=\"--\",\n    label=r\"$\\chi^2_1(0.95)$\"\n)\n\nplt.axvline(\n    p_hat,\n    linestyle=\":\",\n    label=\"best fit\"\n)\n\nplt.axvline(\n    1.0,\n    linestyle=\"-.\",\n    label=\"p = 1\"\n)\n\nif p_left_cross is not None:\n    plt.axvline(\n        p_left_cross,\n        linestyle=\"--\"\n    )\n\nif p_right_cross is not None:\n    plt.axvline(\n        p_right_cross,\n        linestyle=\"--\"\n    )\n\nplt.xlabel(\"p\")\nplt.ylabel(r\"$\\Lambda(p)$\")\n\nplt.title(\n    r\"Adaptive profile likelihood: $p$\"\n)\n\nplt.legend()\nplt.grid(\n    True,\n    alpha=0.3\n)\n\nplt.tight_layout()\n\nplt.savefig(\n    os.path.join(\n        OUTPUT_DIR,\n        \"adaptive_p_profile.png\"\n    ),\n    dpi=220\n)\n\nplt.close()\n\n\n# ============================================================\n# 24. PLOT MONTE CARLO LR\n# ============================================================\n\nplt.figure(\n    figsize=(9, 6)\n)\n\nplt.hist(\n    LR_mc,\n    bins=60\n)\n\nplt.axvline(\n    LR_observed,\n    linestyle=\"--\",\n    linewidth=2,\n    label=\"observed LR\"\n)\n\nplt.axvline(\n    CHI2_95,\n    linestyle=\":\",\n    linewidth=2,\n    label=r\"$\\chi^2_1(95\\%)$\"\n)\n\nplt.xlabel(\"LR statistic\")\nplt.ylabel(\"count\")\n\nplt.title(\n    \"Parametric Monte Carlo test of H0: p = 1\"\n)\n\nplt.legend()\nplt.grid(\n    True,\n    alpha=0.3\n)\n\nplt.tight_layout()\n\nplt.savefig(\n    os.path.join(\n        OUTPUT_DIR,\n        \"monte_carlo_LR.png\"\n    ),\n    dpi=220\n)\n\nplt.close()\n\n\n# ============================================================\n# 25. PLOT p BOOTSTRAP\n# ============================================================\n\nplt.figure(\n    figsize=(9, 6)\n)\n\nplt.hist(\n    boot[\"p\"],\n    bins=60\n)\n\nplt.axvline(\n    1.0,\n    linestyle=\"--\",\n    linewidth=2,\n    label=\"p = 1\"\n)\n\nplt.axvline(\n    p_hat,\n    linestyle=\":\",\n    linewidth=2,\n    label=\"p fitted\"\n)\n\nplt.xlabel(\"p\")\nplt.ylabel(\"count\")\n\nplt.title(\n    \"Residual bootstrap distribution of p\"\n)\n\nplt.legend()\nplt.grid(\n    True,\n    alpha=0.3\n)\n\nplt.tight_layout()\n\nplt.savefig(\n    os.path.join(\n        OUTPUT_DIR,\n        \"bootstrap_p.png\"\n    ),\n    dpi=220\n)\n\nplt.close()\n\n\n# ============================================================\n# 26. PRINT FINAL RESULTS\n# ============================================================\n\nprint(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 80)\nprint(\"FINAL ADAPTIVE PROFILE AUDIT\")\nprint(\"=\" * 80)\n\nprint(\n    f\"\"\"\nFREE MODEL\n\nA       = {A_hat:.12g}\ntheta_c = {theta_c_hat:.12f} deg\np       = {p_hat:.12f}\nB       = {B_hat:.12g}\n\nRSS     = {RSS_hat:.12e}\nRMSE    = {RMSE_hat:.12e}\n\n\nRESTRICTED p=1\n\nA       = {A1:.12g}\ntheta_c = {theta_c_1:.12f} deg\nB       = {B1:.12g}\n\nRSS     = {RSS_1:.12e}\nRMSE    = {RMSE_1:.12e}\n\n\nLIKELIHOOD RATIO\n\nLR observed       = {LR_observed:.12f}\nasymptotic p      = {LR_asymptotic_pvalue:.12e}\nMC p-value        = {mc_pvalue:.12e}\n\n\nADAPTIVE PROFILE theta_c\n\ntheta_c best      = {theta_c_hat:.12f}\n95% lower         = {left_cross}\n95% upper         = {right_cross}\n\n\nADAPTIVE PROFILE p\n\np best            = {p_hat:.12f}\n95% lower         = {p_left_cross}\n95% upper         = {p_right_cross}\n\nDoes profile CI contain p=1?\n    {\n        p_left_cross is not None\n        and p_right_cross is not None\n        and p_left_cross <= 1 <= p_right_cross\n    }\n\n\nDYNAMICAL IDENTITY\n\nC_tau             = {C_tau:.12e}\nrelative std      = {C_tau_rel_std:.12e}\ntau RMSE_log      = {tau_RMSE:.12e}\n\n\nBOOTSTRAP\n\nsuccessful        = {len(boot)}\nsuccess rate      = {len(boot)/N_BOOT:.6f}\n\nbootstrap p:\n    median        = {boot[\"p\"].median():.12f}\n    95% CI        = [\n        {q025(boot[\"p\"]):.12f},\n        {q975(boot[\"p\"]):.12f}\n    ]\n\nbootstrap theta_c:\n    median        = {boot[\"theta_c\"].median():.12f}\n    95% CI        = [\n        {q025(boot[\"theta_c\"]):.12f},\n        {q975(boot[\"theta_c\"]):.12f}\n    ]\n\n\nPARAMETER CORRELATION\n\ncorr(theta_c,p)\n    = {np.corrcoef(\n        boot[\"theta_c\"],\n        boot[\"p\"]\n    )[0,1]:.8f}\n\"\"\"\n)\n\nprint(\"=\" * 80)\nprint(\"OUTPUT DIRECTORY\")\nprint(\"=\" * 80)\n\nfor f in sorted(\n    os.listdir(OUTPUT_DIR)\n):\n    print(\n        os.path.join(\n            OUTPUT_DIR,\n            f\n        )\n    )\n\nprint(\"\\nDONE.\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-14T12:25:32.587903Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-14T12:25:32.588353Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-14T12:26:11.745732Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-09-14T12:25:32.588325Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-14T12:26:11.74509Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"================================================================================\nINPUT\n================================================================================\n/kaggle/input/datasets/fabianleonaressi/krasilnikov-eq8-theta-scan-physical-csv/krasilnikov_eq8_theta_scan_physical.csv\n\n================================================================================\nTERMINAL BRANCH\n================================================================================\nN             = 15\ntheta_min     = -29.600000000000\ntheta_max     = -29.320000000000\n\n================================================================================\nADAPTIVE PROFILE theta_c\n================================================================================\n\n================================================================================\nADAPTIVE PROFILE p\n================================================================================\n\n================================================================================\nRESIDUAL BOOTSTRAP\n================================================================================\n\n================================================